<title>PHILIPPINES: Lippo offers to put money into Manila bank.</title>
<headline>Lippo offers to put money into Manila bank.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's Bank Lippo has offered to pump in one billion pesos to rehabilitate the financially-troubled Monte de Piedad and Savings Bank, the Philippine Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Singson in a statement said banker Vicente Tan, the majority owner of Monte de Piedad, had until 9.35 p.m. (1345 GMT) to match the offer if he still wants to retain his shareholdings in the bank.</p>
</text>
